I have been reading up on the Microsoft Pex documentation and forums and have encountered a few points that might be causing issues:


*

*The class under test (ArrayList) has a base class and the PexFramework should be able to automatically verify the contracts it creates.

*I'm assuming the method signature in the PEXContractTest class has been implemented incorrectly.


Could you help identify the issue in the code?

A: You have a small mistake in your contract tests. Your assumption/expectation might be incorrect. Here are the problems:


*

*You define a new local variable Old_arrListCount to store the count before the action but in your actual code you use the same variable Old_arrListCount as a parameter for your tests methods. Since there is already a parameter named Old_arrListCount, you create another local variable and this makes your test incorrect. 

*Same problem with Others parameters. You can't use any local parameter for testing. All tests must only contain data parameters. 

*You don't observe returned value of arrList.Remove(x) and arrList.Insert(index, x).

*Check if index in arrList.Insert is always less than arrList.Count and greater than or equal to 0.


You should create separated tests for Add, Remove, Insert. Here is an example of correct PUT_AddContract:

[PexMethod]
public void PUT_AddContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
{
    int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int Old_x = x;
    int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
    int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
    bool Old_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    int New_Ret = arrList.Add(x);

    int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int New_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
    int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);

    bool New_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListCount + 1, New_arrListCount);
    Assert.AreEqual(Old_x, x);
    Assert.AreEqual(New_Ret, Old_arrListCount);
    Assert.AreEqual(New_arrListIndexOfX, Old_arrListIndexOfX + 1);
    Assert.AreEqual(New_arrListLastIndexOfX, Old_arrListLastIndexOfX + 1);
    Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListContainsX);
    Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListContainsX, New_arrListContainsX);
}

Also you should avoid using Observe method for debugging. It's better to use Assert.AreEqual or Assert.IsTrue methods for the tests. This will help you understand whether the tests are working fine or not.
Hope it will help you.
